KG42.register("clusters-f9982a2fc42a806cd10ce7dd",{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v142-d-K002","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","label":"Aggregator demand submission, day-ahead welfare clearing and nodal price application","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Aggregator demand submission, day-ahead welfare clearing and nodal price application","market_meaning":"According to whether the load can be deferred, the aggregator submits a demand function or multi-part bids; the DSO performs welfare clearing using the forecast TLMP of the transmission node where the feeder is located as the marginal supply cost, and uses the distribution-node DLMP as the aggregator clearing price within the daily cycle. The current Rule-Chain gives the procedural linkage but not yet a complete computational model.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The three Rule-Chains correspond to the demand information, welfare optimization and price application of the same M02 day-ahead distribution-market procedure. The submission forms for non-deferrable and deferrable loads apply separately and are not merged into a unified bid form.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Submission information, forecast cost, DSO decisions and the aggregator's price use together constitute one market procedure. The correction activity when multiple optimal responses arise after price publication has another trigger condition and outcome target, and is assembled separately in v142-d-K003.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the aggregator submission activity and demand information differentiated by load type."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the DSO's welfare-clearing responsibility and the marginal-cost use of the forecast TLMP."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the price use of the nodal DLMP for the aggregator in this procedure, as the primary attribution of this price-application fact."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E004","v141-b-g01-E005"],"rationale":"The same clearing procedure separately presents the aggregator demand submission and the DSO welfare optimization, supporting the procedural interface between demand information and decision activity; how the specific bids enter the optimization is still not formalized, and step numbers are not converted into new scientific dependency edges."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E006"],"rationale":"The same procedure links the DSO welfare clearing with the aggregator price use of the nodal DLMP; this mapping retains the different roles of the forecast TLMP and the distribution-node DLMP, and does not fabricate a price-calculation formula."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E006"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the DSO that performs optimization and applies prices in the same M02 procedure. Displaying the same entity does not mean merging its different activities."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"M02 lacks a complete objective function, decision variables, feasible constraints, forecast TLMP parameters and an explicit binding from bids to optimization inputs within the same scope, and it also lacks a price-calculation relationship. The existing procedure description is insufficient to compute the allocation and nodal prices.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E004","v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E006"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"In accordance with the existing revision request in R005, additionally submit the day-ahead welfare procedure of Li et al. [12] and the price-formation definition within the same scope, and have C explicitly specify the bindings among submissions, variables, costs and prices; variables or equations from M03 must not be borrowed to fill the gap."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G002","category":"unverified_source","description":"The sources for submission, welfare clearing and price application are all introduction excerpts that have not been independently reviewed; experimental eligibility does not prove that the transcription or scientific interpretation is correct.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E004","v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E006"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the continuous context, day-ahead scope and cited models of the three excerpts, and then check the interpretation of the procedural interface."}]},"rule_refs":["18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R004","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R005","18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG31-67fb13a427efcc14","KG40-45833afd23977831"]});
